      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. the way you described it as \"leveraged to influence the listener's mental state\" is exactly what i'm getting at. it feels much more intentional than just simple hedging. \n\nif these are being used to steer the population toward a state of passive acceptance, how can we identify the \"recovery\" phrases? basically, if someone is caught in that mental lull, what kind of linguistic shift is needed to break that conditioning and force the brain back into an active, questioning mode? i want to start documenting how to counter this.",
